Beam shear, thin walls and section resultants (@mech-beam-shear: 0, is #chapter, #part-of @mechanical-engineering, #source "../sources/Mechanics-of-Materials-Roylance.lingua#r_7K2RYA9504FGFGJTVWHMWXD5WY", #source "../sources/Applied-Mechanics-of-Solids-Bower.lingua#r_109WFZBWMEMGHV9TGFD22H2F1W", #mechanical-engineering "Beam-deflection-and-strain-energy-methods.lingua#r_4N5H6WAFTMCK0SF1TZH0SVF095") { r_5S7AGF32A1MN0G3V5P120G11FV
**Read:** [Modules in Mechanics of Materials — David Roylance](../sources/Mechanics-of-Materials-Roylance.lingua#r_7K2RYA9504FGFGJTVWHMWXD5WY), Stresses in Beams; [Applied Mechanics of Solids — Allan F. Bower](../sources/Applied-Mechanics-of-Solids-Bower.lingua#r_109WFZBWMEMGHV9TGFD22H2F1W), rod theory and linear-elastic solutions. Keep section-resultant equilibrium separate from the local stress assumptions.

A bending moment that changes along the beam implies shear transfer between neighbouring parts of a section. Under the elementary beam assumptions, τ = VQ/(Ib), with Q the first moment of the area on one side of the cut and b its local width. For a rectangular section this gives a parabolic shear profile and maximum 3V/(2A).

For V = 2 kN and a 20×40 mm section, the average shear is 2.5 MPa and the elementary maximum is 3.75 MPa. The maximum bending normal stress and maximum transverse shear generally occur at different locations; combining their separate maxima as though they act at one point can misstate the stress state.

Thin-walled closed sections carry torsion through a shear flow related to the enclosed area. Open sections can be much more compliant and can warp significantly. The shear centre is the load location that avoids torsional coupling in the relevant beam model; it need not coincide with the centroid.

**Work:** Integrate the rectangular shear distribution to recover V. For a flange/web section, identify Q, thickness and the predicted shear flow at each location. Explain how a joint transfers that flow and which local connection stresses the beam approximation does not determine.

